OpenGL style
============
Filtering is the process of accessing a particular sample from a texture. There are two cases for filtering: minification and magnification. 

[a] Magnification means that the area of the fragment in texture space is smaller than a texel.

[b] Minification means that the area of the fragment in texture space is larger than a texel. 

Filtering for these two cases can be set independently.
